# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Liferay workspace lives inside this repo, but almost none of it is source.
# What matters here is client-extensions/ — that is the code an `rm -rf` of the
# workspace once destroyed, and the reason this repo exists.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The downloaded DXP bundle: ~3 GB, reproducible with `blade gw initBundle`.
liferay-workspace/bundles/

# Build output and dependency caches, at any depth.
node_modules/
node_modules_cache/
build/
dist/
.gradle/

# Local runtime noise.
*.log
.DS_Store

# Local environment: contains an OAuth2 client id that is regenerated on every
# deploy anyway, so it is never worth committing. Rebuild it with local-env.sh.
.env

# Python bytecode from the seeder/reset scripts.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Slide decks and presentation artefacts: the DevCon template is a 31 MB org
# asset you re-download, and the built deck plus its render intermediates are
# generated. Binaries like these bloat history fast. The generator and the
# content mapping ARE tracked, so the deck is reproducible from the repo.
*.pptx
*.potx
*.ppt
*.pdf
deck/build/
deck/template/
